WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.074
Internationalization, or i18n,

2
00:00:04.074 --> 00:00:07.580
is the code and design work a
product needs before its first

3
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.659
extra locale.

4
00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:11.520
Localization, or l10n,

5
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.400
is done by translators
and covers translation,

6
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.721
currency, dates, and tone.

7
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:22.560
General Translation handles i18n
in code and generates translations

8
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.767
for each locale.

9
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.296
In code, &lt;T&gt; wraps JSX,

10
00:00:28.296 --> 00:00:31.418
and &lt;Currency&gt; formats
values per locale.

11
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:38.093
Run npx gt translate after you
add a locale in gt.config.json.

12
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.763
Context Groups share terminology,

13
00:00:40.763 --> 00:00:43.560
and reviewers check each
translation in the Dashboard.

14
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:46.610
Your team now ships
German with each release.
